      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors report a case of calcified glomus tumor of the shoulder in a 54-year-old woman. The nonspecific clinical findings and the noncharacteristic imaging results made diagnosis of this tumor impossible before surgery. The diagnosis was confirmed by a biopsy. The outcome after surgical resection was excellent."},
